# SRG-APP-000099-AU-000720  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must produce audit records that contain information
# to establish the outcome of the events.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000099-AU-000720
group:           V-221912
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000134
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk's own audit records carry the outcome of each audited operation and
                 reach a searchable index when the audit trail is queued to the index.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        The sending hosts and devices must state the outcome in the records they
                 transmit; Splunk extracts and classifies what it receives and cannot infer
                 an outcome the sender omitted.
external:        Where queueing is deliberately set to false, the audit log is still
                 written to disk and the records reach an index only through a separate
                 monitor input, which the assessor confirms in inputs.conf.

citation:        OVER-REACH and INVENTION, as at SRG-APP-000095-AU-000680. Removed
                 eventtypes.conf [<eventtype>] search non_empty: the shipped
                 eventtypes.conf declares "search =" empty in its default stanza and ships
                 no event types, so the condition fails a stock instance; event types are
                 an optional search-time feature that neither the check nor the fix text
                 requires. Also removed props.conf [<spec>] <spec> present, which named the
                 spec-file placeholder as both stanza and key - props.conf has no such
                 setting, so it could never match - and whose determined form is a
                 whole-file presence test every installation passes. Outcome is carried in
                 the record text and read by field extraction, which no single props.conf
                 key decides.
finding:         The audit trail is not queued to an index (queueing = false) with no
                 compensating input, so the outcome recorded on each audited operation is
                 not searchable in the repository.
